  <header class="page-hero shell"><p class="section-label">About / Ilian Aigner</p><h1>Ambitious.<br />Still learning.</h1><p>I’m serious about becoming exceptional at sales. Here’s the person doing the work.</p></header>
  <section class="content-section shell about-intro"><img class="about-portrait" src="/assets/images/ilian-portrait-shirt-700.jpg" width="700" height="700" alt="Portrait of Ilian Aigner in a navy suit" loading="lazy" /><div><p>I’m an entrepreneurship student at the University of Delaware, working toward a B.S. with minors in Professional Sales &amp; Sales Management and Marketing. I expect to graduate in Fall 2028.</p><p>I’m not learning sales casually. I want to understand what makes a client act, explain complex ideas clearly, and earn trust when it matters. The Lerner Sales Competition put that ambition under pressure. Horbach gave me a closer look at client conversations. STRK gives me something of my own to build.</p><p>Before Delaware, I coached basketball in Hamburg. Working with children and teenagers taught me to change the explanation without lowering the standard. Away from work, I’m drawn to basketball, travel, and conversations that take me outside my own perspective. I speak German, English, and French.</p><p>I’m seeking a U.S. B2B sales, SDR, or BDR internship where I can learn quickly and contribute early.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/#contact">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="about-places shell" aria-labelledby="places-heading"><p class="section-label">The places behind the work</p><h2 id="places-heading">I carry Hamburg<br />{' '}into Delaware.</h2><div class="about-places-grid"><div><span>Home</span><h3>Hamburg</h3><p>Where I coached basketball and learned to adjust my communication to the person in front of me.</p></div><div><span>Now</span><h3>Delaware</h3><p>Where I’m studying entrepreneurship, testing myself in sales, and building STRK beyond the classroom.</p></div></div><p class="about-aside">Outside the work: basketball, travel, and conversations in German, English, or French.</p></section>
